# Geospatial File Measurement API

## Project Overview
This project will provide an API that accepts KML files and zipped Shapefiles and calculates measurements for geographic features, including polygon areas and line lengths.

## Planned Functionality
- KML file processing
- Shapefile ZIP processing
- Feature and geometry detection
- CRS detection
- Reprojection to an appropriate projected CRS
- Polygon area calculation
- Line length calculation
- Per-feature measurement results
- API endpoints for file information and measurements
- Graceful handling of invalid or unsupported geometries

## Technology Stack
Planned technologies:
- Frontend: React
- Backend: FastAPI / Python
- GeoPandas
- Shapely
- pyproj
- Database: to be decided

## Project Structure
- `client/` — planned location for the frontend
- `server/` — planned location for the backend API
- `README.md` — project overview, plans, and status
- `.gitignore` — files and directories to exclude from version control

## Development Plan
1. Basic client and server setup
2. File upload
3. KML processing
4. Shapefile processing
5. Geometry handling
6. CRS handling and reprojection
7. Measurement calculation
8. Result storage
9. API endpoints
10. Testing
11. Error handling
12. Documentation and finalization

## Current Status
Initial project structure only. Implementation will be added incrementally.